 "text": "..title\nAn ordinance authorizing the granting of a permanent easement to the Nashville Metropolitan Transit Authority on certain property owned by the Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County (Proposal No. 2026M-024AG-001). \n..body\nWHEREAS, the Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County owns real property located at 1500 Dickerson Pike, Nashville, Tennessee (Parcel No. 07111000400) (the \"Property\"); and, \nWHEREAS, the Nashville Metropolitan Transit Authority, doing business as \"WeGo,\" has requested an easement, as described in the Easement Agreement attached hereto and incorporated herein as Exhibit A, on the area designated as shown on Exhibit A for the purpose of constructing, maintaining, repairing, rebuilding, operating, and patrolling a Bus Stop Shelter; and, \nWHEREAS, the Board of Education has approved the granting of the easement.\nNOW, THEREFORE, BE IT ENACTED BY THE COUNCIL OF THE METROPOLITAN GOVERNMENT OF NASHVILLE AND DAVIDSON COUNTY, TENNESSEE:\nSection 1. \tThe granting of the easement to the Nashville Metropolitan Transit Authority, as described in the Easement Agreement attached hereto and incorporated herein as Exhibit A, is hereby approved. \n   Parcel No.\n   Address - Location\n     Easement Type\n   Exhibit\n07111000400\n1500 Dickerson Pike\nPermanent\nA\nSection 2.\tThe Director of Public Property Administration is authorized to grant said easement and to execute the necessary documents pertaining thereto.\nSection 3.\tThis ordinance shall take effect from and after its final passage, the welfare of the Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County, Tennessee, requiring it.\n..Agenda Analysis\nAnalysis\n\nThis ordinance grants permanent and temporary construction easements to Nashville Metropolitan Transit Authority (\"WeGo Public Transit\") on property owned by the Metropolitan Government at 1500 Dickerson Pike, the site of Shwab Elementary School.\n\nThese easements were requested by WeGo Public Transit for the purpose of constructing, maintaining, repairing, rebuilding, operating, and patrolling a bus stop shelter.\n\nThis proposal was approved by the Planning Commission.\n\nFiscal Note: This ordinance authorizes Metro to grant an easement on the property located at 1500 Dickerson Pike to the Nashville Metropolitan Transit Authority (\"WeGo\") for the purpose of constructing of a bus stop shelter. The easement is conveyed for consideration in the amount of $1.00.\n\n"
}
